      {
        "id": 3913435240,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "Location: `src/craft/brew.c` `can_brew_spell()` line 590, and the check that still runs afterward in `do_brew()` at lines 1087-1091. `brew_resolve()` lines 87-94 repeat that check.\n\nExploit/repro: Level 11 artificer, Artificer Item Creation, no other class levels. `artificer_can_emulate_spell()` is true for mage armor (wizard level 1, circle 1, device cap 4). `brew 'mage armor'` does not start brewing. It prints:\n\n```\nChecking spell availability...\nYou don't have 'mage armor' prepared or you lack the spell slots to cast it.\n```\n\nAn artificer has no spell collection and no spell slots, so every device spell the new branch accepts dies here. Fireball at the same level (circle 3, also emulable) gets the same refusal. `can_brew_spell()` returning true is not enough.\n\nFix: When `artificer_can_emulate_spell(ch, spell)` is true, skip `spell_prep_gen_check()` in `do_brew()`, skip the `verify_spells` recheck in `brew_resolve()`, and do not call `spell_prep_gen_extract()` for that spell. The alchemy check is the emulation roll.",
        "author": {
          "id": 42759441,
          "username": "max757",
          "public_email": "",
          "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
          "state": "active",
          "locked": false,
          "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c7c169343bd7d0f4575137ce8065aee7cb44024d447bbfe66d773133a81c43e?s=80&d=identicon",
