      {
        "id": 3913946472,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "Valid; fixed in 36953d692. When `artificer_can_emulate_spell()` is true, `do_brew()` skips `spell_prep_gen_check()` and prints `--<spell> is emulated`. `brew_resolve()` also skips the `verify_spells` recheck and does not call `spell_prep_gen_extract()`; it prints `<spell> emulated (no spell slot used)`. Tests: `Test_artificer_brews_emulated_spells_without_slots` (a level 11 artificer brewing mage armor starts the brew activity) and `Test_artificer_brew_completion_needs_no_slot` (a verified resolution stores the potion). Both fail on the old code.",
