      {
        "id": 3913435324,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "Location: `src/craft/brew.c` `create_multi_spell_potion()` lines 821-823. `brew_resolve()` builds a physical potion only by calling that function (line 282). `create_potion()` lines 734-736 repeat the same feat check, and `brew_resolve()` does not call it.\n\nExploit/repro: Wizard 9 / Artificer 20 with Artificer Item Creation. Heal undead is wizard level 9, circle 5, and `MAG_MANUAL` rather than `MAG_DAMAGE`, so `can_brew_spell()` does not reject it as offensive and `artificer_can_emulate_spell()` is false (device cap is circle 4). `create_multi_spell_potion()` with that one spell returns a potion whose `GET_OBJ_VAL(potion, 0)` is 20, the artificer level, not the wizard caster level 9. Captured run: `wizard_min=9 circle=5 mag_damage=0 emulate=0 potion_caster_level=20`.\n\nFix: Take the artificer level only when `artificer_can_emulate_spell(ch, spell)` is true for a spell in the potion. Otherwise leave the caster level chosen from the spellcasting classes (9 here). Apply the same condition in `create_potion()`.",
        "author": {
          "id": 42759441,
          "username": "max757",
          "public_email": "",
          "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
          "state": "active",
