  {
    "id": "7749c22756c8ffbbe953d5cf2b6f36d79fc2b0bf",
    "individual_note": true,
    "resolvable": false,
    "notes": [
      {
        "id": 3913959797,
        "type": null,
        "body": "Merged as 962463fa6 (merge commit, 10 commits, not squashed; the branch was 0 behind master).\n\n**What merged**\n- The reported bug: `device add` now accepts 3rd- and 4th-circle spells under the same circle cap and per-circle budget as `device create`.\n- The other 25 artificer defects from #4: device persistence, `device use` stopping on a dead target, Metamagic Science charges and UMD checks, create/repair cancel, craft-roll feats, starting kit, golem feat levels, Brilliance and Blunder as a gnome racial, explosion damage and death, circle assignment, premade build, and help.\n- Review fixes (36953d692): an artificer brews device spells without spell slots and ahead of the alchemist level cap, and a potion takes the artificer level only when one of its spells is a device spell.\n- 21 tests in `unittests/CuTest/test_artificer_devices.c`. The full local CI matrix passed (33 jobs).\n\n**Follow-up**\n- Production help is not synced. `class-artificer`, `devices`, `gnomes`, and `class-roster` are in the dev help DB and `help.hlp` only. Run help-sync to publish them.\n- Existing gnomes get Brilliance and Blunder only on respec.\n- Items 3 (device use after the target dies) and 9 (starting kit) have no unit test. The live check on port 4100 covered both.",
        "author": {
          "id": 42759441,
          "username": "max757",
          "public_email": "",
          "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
          "state": "active",
          "locked": false,
